# Objectif Français — Project Rules

## What this is
French vocabulary learning web app. Replaces WordBit. Built on Lexique 3.83 (46,792 words, CC-BY-SA).

## Stack
React + Vite, Supabase (future), Vercel deployment

## Dictionary
- Source: /data/lexique383_full.json
- 46,792 unique lemmas, frequency-ranked from spoken French subtitle corpus
- Fields: w (word), l (lemma), p (phonetic), g (grammar), gn (gender), lv (CEFR), fs (spoken freq), fw (written freq), sy (syllables), mr (morph root), fm (family members)
- CEFR levels assigned by frequency rank: top 500=A1, next 1000=A2, next 2000=B1, next 3500=B2, next 8000=C1, rest=C2
- No English translations yet — need to add

## Core features (implemented in V3)
- Email/password auth with persistent sessions
- Rapid Review: scroll through words one-by-one, tap know/don't know (WordBit removed this feature — we restore it)
- Quiz mode: identify words by phonetics and grammar
- Family Quiz: test word family connections
- Chain learning: knowing a root gives 70% credit to derived words, knowing a family member in "learning" state gives 30%
- Spaced repetition: 3-pass system, expanding intervals (1→2→4→8→16→30 days)
- Bulk import: mark words as known in batches (for transitioning from WordBit)
- Search + filter by CEFR level and grammar category
- Roots & Patterns screen teaching suffix/prefix rules

## Exam targeting
- All paths use TCF Canada (NCLC scoring)
- Francophone Mobility: NCLC 5+ speaking & listening
- PR/Express Entry: NCLC 7+ all four skills
- Citizenship: NCLC 4+ speaking & listening
- Personal: no exam, learn at own pace

## Regions
- FR (France), CA (Canada — not just Quebec, includes NB, Nova Scotia, etc.), BE (Belgique), AF (Afrique francophone)
- Canada is the default region

## Key design decisions
- Zero ads, ever
- Anonymous-first: study without login, login to save progress
- Frequency over CEFR: show real spoken frequency, not arbitrary textbook levels
- Dual system: general frequency rank + domain priority (immigration words surface first if goal is Francophone Mobility)
- Word families are navigable: tap a family member to jump to it
- Gender shown with color coding (blue=masc, pink=fem)

## What to build next (priority order)
1. Load full 46,792-word dictionary from JSON instead of hardcoded 80-word array
2. English translations for at least top 3,000 words
3. Deploy to Vercel
4. Audio/TTS pronunciation with adjustable speed
5. Supabase auth + progress sync
6. False friends database (vrais amis, faux amis, semi-faux amis, faux-faux amis)
7. Domain vocabulary modules (tech/phone, workplace, immigration, housing, healthcare)
8. Exam mode with TCF Canada parameters
9. Timed rapid review for listening speed training

## Never do
- Add ads or ad SDKs
- Remove the rapid review feature
- Require login to study
- Duplicate words across CEFR levels
- Use textbook ordering instead of frequency ranking
